TRANSFER TEST: THM-2922 window machinery -> shell-imbalance module

1. Size of the variety cut out by the equations
   SFC side : L(H^k)=0, k=1..4, NONLINEAR in the coefficients,
              coefficients free over C -> a genuine intersection.
   shell side: c^(2m) = -c^(m)*(1+u)^(2m) is LINEAR and c^(m) is free.
     m=  1: solution space over Q has dimension 1   (equations impose 0 conditions)
     m=  2: solution space over Q has dimension 3   (equations impose 0 conditions)
     m=  4: solution space over Q has dimension 7   (equations impose 0 conditions)
     m=  8: solution space over Q has dimension 15   (equations impose 0 conditions)
     m= 16: solution space over Q has dimension 31   (equations impose 0 conditions)

   => the compensation EQUATIONS cut out nothing.  Every obstruction
      is in the integer box, which elimination theory cannot see.

2. Where the box actually binds (least-overflow witness)
   m=2: min over admissible c of max_i |c2_i|/N2_i = 2 = 2.0000 > 1
        first binding index i=4 of 0..8   (middle index is 4)   witness c=[0, -2, 2, 0, 0]
   m=4: min over admissible c of max_i |c2_i|/N2_i = 3/2 = 1.5000 > 1
        first binding index i=7 of 0..16   (middle index is 8)   witness c=[0, -4, 6, -4, 0, 4, -6, 4, 0]

VERDICT.  The core of THM-2922 does NOT transfer.  Its Macaulay
resultant chart and Gregory-Newton minors exist to prove that a NONLINEAR
system over an UNCONSTRAINED coefficient space has only the trivial solution.
Our system is LINEAR and its solution space is full-dimensional; the whole
obstruction is the integer box, i.e. a lattice-point question, on which
resultants are silent.  The two difficulties are exactly complementary.

TWO PERIPHERAL STEPS DO TRANSFER.
 (a) MEAN ELIMINATION.  THM-2922 kills the first moment with the differences
     f_a - f_(a+5).  Our analogue is already proved independently:
     N_0 = N_2m = 0 and C^(m)(1) = 0 force C^(m)(u) = 2u(1-u)G(u).  Same move.
 (b) POSITIVITY CERTIFICATES IN THE FAMILY PARAMETER.  THM-2922 proves its
     statement for ALL translations n by exhibiting Gregory-Newton positive
     certificates in n.  That is precisely what the shell module still needs:
     the non-compensation is verified only at m = 1, 2, 4, and a certificate
     positive in m would give all dyadic m at once.  This is the one genuinely
     importable idea, and it is NOT yet done.
